{
  "area": "curacao",
  "method": "Curaçao and Klein Curaçao, ordered from Klein Curaçao and the east point along the south coast to Westpunt. No official site list exists: CARMABI and the Curaçao Marine Park publish no named-site or mooring list, so the Curaçao Tourist Board's dive-and-snorkel site list (curacao.com) stands in as the one non-operator list. Operator lists read: Ocean Encounters (also LionsDive), GO WEST Diving (also All West Apartments; boat schedule and shore-diving pages counted as one list), Fundiving Curaçao, Scuba Do, Dive Curaçao (Dive Center Lagun and Pietermaai), Scubaçao and Blue Bay Dive; each counts as one list. Not counted: DivePlannerPro pages (a platform's 'reachable from' aggregate, not the shop's list), caribseasports.com (a numbered list on a domain now carrying casino spam), Wannadive (Bonaire only now), and guides, blogs and PADI/SSI directories, read for leads only. A site is counted when it is named, recreationally divable on scuba and on at least two independent lists. Where a list sells several features as one dive (Smokey's with Kathy's Paradise; Marie Pampoen with Car Pile, Pierbaai and Oswaldo's Drop-off) it is one row with the features as aliases. Region names (Westpoint, Caracasbaai) and one-list names are kept as excluded rows. Eastpoint is counted because four operators sell it as a named dive. The tourist board's 'Playa Hundu Lost Anchor' entry describes a deserted cove, so it is credited to Playa Hundu only; its 'Kas Abou/Lower House' to Cas Abou; its 'Airplane Wreck' (Santa Martha) to Santa Martha; its 'Playa Kenepa' to Grote Knip. Counted 2026-10-14.",
